      "message": "What about doing something like:\n\n  def _expand_project_list(self, request, ref):\n      params \u003d request.params\n\n      tagged_projects \u003d []\n      tag_map \u003d {\n          \u0027tags\u0027: \u0027list_projects_with_tags\u0027,\n          \u0027tags-any\u0027: \u0027list_projects_with_tags_any\u0027,\n          \u0027not-tags\u0027: \u0027list_projects_not_tags\u0027,\n          \u0027not-tags-any\u0027: \u0027list_projects_not_tags_any\u0027\n      }\n      for k, v in tag_map.items():\n          tag_set  \u003d params[k]\n          if k in params and self.query_filter_is_true(tag_set):\n              tagged_projects.append(getattr(self.resource_api, v)(tag_set))\n      return tagged_projects\n\nThis was totally back of the napkin, so it might need some ironing. This way you might not need as many if statements to get the same result. You also don\u0027t have to convert form tag to boolean back to tag.",
